Id: misc026w
Severity: WARN
Category: filesystem
Check: check_umask
Fix: Set UMASK 022 (or 027) in /etc/login.defs.
References: login.defs(5); pam_umask(8)
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST AC-3, CM-6; ISO 8.9; CE Secure configuration

/etc/login.defs has no UMASK setting, so the default file creation mask
for login sessions is whatever the shell start-up files or PAM provide, if
anything. Set UMASK 022 (or 027 where users should not read each other's
files) in /etc/login.defs; with pam_umask in the PAM session stack that
value applies to every login.
